ranch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841133: Add null-checks for mTransport in WebTransport r=necko-reviewers,kershaw a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182573", "files": ["dom/webtransport/child/WebTransportChild.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9e4dda6620bd0d639658a5b515b237dd1044432b", "parents": ["97cb893b496bafbce24aba14edbae0a13356c541"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1839073, r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D181779", "files": ["toolkit/modules/PopupNotifications.sys.mjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ea939ed893bc4353cc8980248c859a7ed4f79c08", "parents": ["9e4dda6620bd0d639658a5b515b237dd1044432b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1837686. r=jandem,rhunt a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182324", "files": ["js/src/jit/AliasAnalysis.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2ddcad48ab61fbfb15e038456ac46274e9b97f94", "parents": ["ea939ed893bc4353cc8980248c859a7ed4f79c08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1782561 - Do not use getter_AddRefs to pass object to function r=necko-reviewers,cookie-reviewers,jesup,edgul, a=RyanVM\n\nWhen using getter_AddRefs it actually nulls out the pointer before\npassing it to the function, so in this case a new list was being\ncreated with every call to CreateOrUpdatePurgeList.\nInstead, we can just pass a reference to the `nsCOMPtr\u003cnsIArray\u003e&`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D181743", "files": ["netwerk/cookie/CookieStorage.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieStorage.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "888192f3f6bee95310eb1d5deee7f06e5d2bf472", "parents": ["2ddcad48ab61fbfb15e038456ac46274e9b97f94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1782561 - Make sure we can evict cookies while processing AddCookie r=necko-reviewers,cookie-reviewers,jesup,edgul, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D181744", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b068997628430b221554b48d0c7eea90ff3a9083", "parents": ["888192f3f6bee95310eb1d5deee7f06e5d2bf472"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689188902, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "33": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1830070: Correctly apply RFP Checks to about: documents and deal with pop-ups (ESR) r=smaug,emilio, a=dsmith\n\n\nThis patch has three parts to it, in addition to the many tests\nit adds:\n\n1) Use NS_IsContentAccessibleAboutURI to ensure that only safe\n   about: documents get exempted.\n\n   With this change, we will no longer allow about:blank or\n   about:srcdoc to be exempted base on URI.  If they are to be\n   exempted, it will need to be base on other information.\n\n2) In Document::RecomputeResistFingerprinting we previously\n   deferred to a Parent Document if we had one, and either the\n   principals matched or we were a null principal.\n\n   We will do the same thing, except we will also defer to our\n   opener as well as the parent document.  Now about:blank\n   documents can be exempted.\n\n   However, this deferral only works if the opener is\n   same-process. For cross-process openers, we make the decision\n   ourselves.\n\nWe can make the wrong decision though. CookieJarSettings is\ninherited through iframes but it is _not_ inherited through popups.\n(Yet. There's some discussion there, but it's not implemented.)\n\nConceptually; however, we do want CJS to inherit, and we do want\nRFP to inherit as well.  Because a popup can collude with its\nopener to bypass RFP and Storage restrictions, we should propagate\nthe CJS information.\n\nThis does lead to an unusual situation: if you have exempted\nb.com, and a.com (which is not exempted) creates a popup for b.com\nthen that popup will not be exempted.  But an open tab for b.com\nwould be.  And it might be hard to tell those two apart, or why\nthey behave differently.\n\nThe third part of the patch:\n\n3) In LoadInfo we want to populate information down from the\n   opener to the popup.  This is needed because otherwise a\n   cross-origin popup will not defer to its opener (because in\n   Fission they're in different processes) and will decide if\n   it should be exempted itself. It's the CookieJarSettings\n   object that prevents the cross-origin document from thinking\n   it should be exempted - CJS tells it 'No, you're a child\n   (either a subdocument or a popup) and if I say you don't get\n   an exemption, you don't.'\n\n\nFinally, there is one more caveat: we can only defer to a parent\ndocument or opener if it still exists.  A popup may outlive its\nopener. If that happens, and something induces a call to\nRecomputeResistFingerprinting, then (e.g.) an about:blank popup\nmay lose an RFP exemption that it had received from its parent.\nThis isn't expected to happen in practice -\nRecomputeResistFingerprinting is only called on document creation\nand pref changes I believe.\n\nIt is not possible for a popup to _gain_ an exemption though,\nbecause even if the parent document is gone, the CJS lives on and\nrestricts it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183189", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.ini", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_aboutblank.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_blob.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_blob_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_data.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_data_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/file_hwconcurrency_aboutblank_popupmaker.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/file_hwconcurrency_blob_popupmaker.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/file_hwconcurrency_data_popupmaker.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/file_hwconcurrency_iframee.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/file_hwconcurrency_iframer.html", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/head.js", "caps/BasePrincipal.cpp", "caps/BasePrincipal.h", "caps/nsIPrincipal.idl", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "netwerk/base/LoadInfo.cpp", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/docs/implementation.rst"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ac88490d08ba5805269f581f71078271d3da9b2c", "parents": ["b068997628430b221554b48d0c7eea90ff3a9083"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842325. Ensure that WebRenderLayerManager::mTarget is always cleared after a transaction. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman, a=dsmith\n\nThe scope exit in WebRenderLayerManager::EndTransactionWithoutLayer isn't necessary because there are no early returns in that function, but I added it just in case an early return is added in the future.\n\nThe assert in nsDisplayList::PaintRoot currently holds because of how the current code is, but these changes will mean EndEmptyTransaction will handle that case as far as clearing mTarget is concerned.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183069", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2aec0839b075541f36208354765cf4ca040a6745", "parents": ["ac88490d08ba5805269f581f71078271d3da9b2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841216: Fire a11y description change event when aria-description is changed. r=nlapre, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182544", "files": ["accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_description.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "423af88badecff986ed286c6321d88218cd046b0", "parents": ["2aec0839b075541f36208354765cf4ca040a6745"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tomislav Jovanovic \u003ctomica@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842009 - Don't send session area storage.onChanged events to content scripts r=robwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183256", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-storage.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_storage_session.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dc7a19fb472e28ab0fabc98cf2cc523c639d334b", "parents": ["423af88badecff986ed286c6321d88218cd046b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840701 - [marionette] TcpTransport:receive needs to return immediately when socket was closed. r=webdriver-reviewers,jgraham, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182622", "files": ["testing/marionette/client/marionette_driver/transport.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "54929bac22f0a4187834377475ae2510a87b065f", "parents": ["dc7a19fb472e28ab0fabc98cf2cc523c639d334b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183486", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/devtools-compatibility-browsers.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eb27025de6cdf737203a4133b81f44641c59b434", "parents": ["54929bac22f0a4187834377475ae2510a87b065f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689260777, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "34": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1825561: Add in the ETP Toggle check to the ShouldRFP callgraph. r=timhuang, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183523", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser.ini", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_etp_iframes.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_aboutblank.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_aboutsrcdoc.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_blob.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_blobcrossorigin.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_data.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_iframes_sandboxediframe.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_aboutblank.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_blob.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_blob_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_data.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_data_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_hwconcurrency_popups_noopener.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/head.js", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/docs/implementation.rst"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "26391d532b16b1801beaa60b758e233738283319", "parents": ["eb27025de6cdf737203a4133b81f44641c59b434"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1835099: Check the Partition Key in both flows. r=timhuang, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183524\n\nDepends on D183523", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser.ini", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_fpiServiceWorkers_fingerprinting.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/serviceWorker.js", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/docs/implementation.rst"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "01a2b291ead0be95d3c8d1c819bcf05b9e124f26", "parents": ["26391d532b16b1801beaa60b758e233738283319"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842678: Exempt non-content about: urls and add debug logging. r=timhuang, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183525\n\nDepends on D183524", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cb4eb7a6d30843c3d0dc29c143d83a004a1b6856", "parents": ["01a2b291ead0be95d3c8d1c819bcf05b9e124f26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Xi Ruoyao \u003cxry111@xry111.site\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841040 - Remove over-alignment from GCMarker and Nursery, r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco a=RyanVM\n\njs_new\u003cT\u003e cannot guarantee the alignment if T is over-aligned, and this\nissue is not trivial to fix (blocked by Bug 1842582).\n\nAdd a static assert to detect the attempt using js_new\u003cT\u003e for\nover-aligned T, and remove the problematic alignas() attributes as a\nshort-term fix.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182546", "files": ["js/public/Utility.h", "js/src/gc/GCMarker.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d8f7dc382591a769ad1938e30bcadad3efaa9287", "parents": ["cb4eb7a6d30843c3d0dc29c143d83a004a1b6856"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842933 - Use NEON_FLAGS instead of VPX_ASFLAGS for libaom neon code. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,andi a=RyanVM\n\nBack when libaom was added, VPX_ASFLAGS was more or less the only\nvariable that had the right set of flags for NEON support, which\njustified its use. However, it's not set when building against system\nlibvpx.\n\nBug 1791482 improved things, though, and VPX_ASFLAGS, as far as NEON is\nconcerned, is now only re-exporting NEON_FLAGS, with the same caveat that\nVPX_ASFLAGS is empty when building against system libvpx.\n\nSo we should use NEON_FLAGS instead of VPX_ASFLAGS.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183310", "files": ["media/libaom/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8cfd1d58d8998d95762b3e6303dc6354d9fab324", "parents": ["d8f7dc382591a769ad1938e30bcadad3efaa9287"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689350786, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "35": {"changesets": [{"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1824634 disconnect from GtkIMContext OnDestroyWindow  a=RyanVM\n\nwhich will allow a GtkIMContext to outlive the IMContextWrapper.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182865\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183446", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7ce9193147e62870a41b6e5995ca146de6bfa362", "parents": ["8cfd1d58d8998d95762b3e6303dc6354d9fab324"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1824634 hold GtkIMContext reference a little longer than preedit-changed  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182866\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183447", "files": ["widget/gtk/GRefPtr.h", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8fe4702175c3da3e34083904c533f1deee3c3f24", "parents": ["7ce9193147e62870a41b6e5995ca146de6bfa362"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689355914, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "36": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842432 - Fix ChannelMediaDecoder::ComputePlaybackRate. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183249", "files": ["dom/media/ChannelMediaDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ea6e2e85fec64e26f28f95f930063d47f23c4573", "parents": ["8fe4702175c3da3e34083904c533f1deee3c3f24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842949 - Delegate IPC call to a main-thread runnable if necessary. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman,a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183377", "files": ["gfx/thebes/SharedFontList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4b150112debe889f47fcf7d2c238897c9291b24f", "parents": ["ea6e2e85fec64e26f28f95f930063d47f23c4573"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840792 - Be more resilient and timely when dealing with database corruption during Chrome browser import. r=kpatenio, a=dsmith\n\nThis patch does two things:\n\n1. It makes it so that a corrupt database doesn't result in several retries to\n   requery the database, as it's extremely unlikely that a corrupt database is\n   going to somehow get repaired in the interim.\n2. It makes it so that if any Chrome-based browser resource fails to be acquired\n   properly, it still allows other resources from the same (and other!) profiles\n   to be imported.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D182737", "files": ["browser/components/migration/ChromeProfileMigrator.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/MigrationUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/Library/Application Support/Google/Chrome/Default/HistoryCorrupt", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/head_migration.js", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/test_Chrome_bookmarks.js", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/test_Chrome_corrupt_history.js", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/xpcshell.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8ddf1677de1814775f52e8f9ad8b65ce1ea9a659", "parents": ["4b150112debe889f47fcf7d2c238897c9291b24f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shane Hughes \u003cshughes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1832715 - Allow multistage spotlight OPEN_URL actions to include UTM params. r=omc-reviewers,negin, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D177848", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/newtab/content-src/asrouter/templates/FirstRun/addUtmParams.js", "browser/components/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/addUtmParams.test.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "43db2f5e45bba449783ae8d66db1bd7f7ecee385", "parents": ["8ddf1677de1814775f52e8f9ad8b65ce1ea9a659"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842658 - Part 2: Use refcounting macros for nsHtml5OwningUTF16Buffer, r=mccr8, a=dsmith\n\nWhen the code was originally added in bug 1842658, it was to use non-atomic\nrefcounting across multiple threads due to some invariants preventing\nconcurrent access. That was changed in bug 1607762 to fix a race issue.\n\nWe should be able to switch to using the macros now, which will simplify the\ncode here a bit.\n\nDepends on D183203\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183204", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5OwningUTF16Buffer.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5OwningUTF16Buffer.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b320eac319c0cba02c1d0e301e06e62c83137bf7", "parents": ["43db2f5e45bba449783ae8d66db1bd7f7ecee385"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1838792: Add TryAddStoredObject to DrawEventRecorderPrivate and use in DrawTargetRecording. r=aosmond, a=dsmith\n\nThis means we can do a combination of HasStoredObject and AddStoredObject with\nonly one call to ProcessPendingDeletions, which uses locking.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D181963", "files": ["gfx/2d/DrawEventRecorder.h", "gfx/2d/DrawTargetRecording.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5a6e1e04029afacb9f21b7b6781cf36c8d340f64", "parents": ["b320eac319c0cba02c1d0e301e06e62c83137bf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1831467 - Avoid more UB from transmuting a ref to a ref with interior mutability. r=emilio, a=dsmith\n\naka one specific change in LLVM 16 introducing UB in Rust, take 3? 4?\n\nThis time, we have multiple types like:\n  #[xpcom(implement(nsISomething))]\n  struct Foo {\n      foo: RefCell\u003cSomething\u003e,\n  }\n\n  impl Foo {\n      fn from_interface(obj: &nsISomething) -\u003e &Self {\n          unsafe { ::std::mem::transmute(obj) }\n      }\n  }\n\nAt first glance, this looks innocuous. But the problem is that\nnsISomething, as far as LLVM is informed by Rust, is readonly,\nbut Foo, via the RefCell, has interious mutability.\n\nLLVM ends up assuming that any mutability that happens to that returned\n&Foo can't happen, and removes it.\n\nThis is yet another case where https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/111229\nwould save our feet from this footgun LLVM 16 added and that the rust\ncompiler doesn't help us prevent the least.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183569\n***\nBug 1831467 fix comment a=dsmith", "files": ["xpcom/idl-parser/xpidl/rust.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8050da8633666737372950daf291f58930e6af76", "parents": ["5a6e1e04029afacb9f21b7b6781cf36c8d340f64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183746", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "77b137f05f8515e81b6c39fe28184619b716173f", "parents": ["8050da8633666737372950daf291f58930e6af76"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689609470, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "37": {"changesets": [{"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842437 - re-apply the YouTube webcompat intervention to fix back-forward cache navigation issues; r=denschub,webcompat-reviewers, a=RyanVM", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/injections.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/injections/js/bug1842437-www.youtube.com-performance-now-precision.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/moz.build"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ed0517f7877b8e92929252dcfc9feee501519d86", "parents": ["77b137f05f8515e81b6c39fe28184619b716173f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842792, disable speculative load of modulepreload if parser has seen importmap, r=jonco,allstarschh,peterv, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183421", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderHSupplement.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "80a254bffd37bf887efbfd566274191ff3098cd7", "parents": ["ed0517f7877b8e92929252dcfc9feee501519d86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843086: Line participants use block start ascent, instead of not-yet stored baseline. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183432", "files": ["layout/generic/nsLineLayout.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/baseline-source/baseline-source-inline-box-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/baseline-source/baseline-source-inline-box.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6c69caf5d86267982c4191ccbf4294098c67f8b1", "parents": ["80a254bffd37bf887efbfd566274191ff3098cd7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689628220, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "38": {"changesets": [{"author": "donal meehan \u003cdmeehan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_115_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Set version to 115.0.3, a=me", "files": ["browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5d2ffa4fb7d07a9afa9ecb9f2f9619c4e72fb5c9", "parents": ["872b5aae170ffa755f89d0c6a9ebc380af677e9a"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_115_0_3esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_115_0_3esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1689695488, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "39": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 5d2ffa4fb7d07a9afa9ecb9f2f9619c4e72fb5c9 with FIREFOX_115_0_3esr_BUILD1 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f9ffbda2ebb92f82ae179f3a50d46c2f54304e8e", "parents": ["6c69caf5d86267982c4191ccbf4294098c67f8b1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689707804, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "40": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 5d2ffa4fb7d07a9afa9ecb9f2f9619c4e72fb5c9 with FIREFOX_115_0_3esr_RELEASE a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3aff061847d162b2c606a7df232bfb38afe78a67", "parents": ["f9ffbda2ebb92f82ae179f3a50d46c2f54304e8e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689719239, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "41": {"changesets": [{"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843847. Clear nsDisplayListBuilder::mCurrentContainerASR at the end of a paint. r=mstange, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183741", "files": ["layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bfcbc3a3117857753bf7a59f071bb38a761a00fd", "parents": ["3aff061847d162b2c606a7df232bfb38afe78a67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843038 - Make CypherStrategy::DeserializeKey fallible, r=janv, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183509", "files": ["dom/quota/CipherStrategy.h", "dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream_impl.h", "dom/quota/DummyCipherStrategy.h", "dom/quota/NSSCipherStrategy.cpp", "dom/quota/NSSCipherStrategy.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3a68be3f458d47d42871857cc4790d32bb0ef8a5", "parents": ["bfcbc3a3117857753bf7a59f071bb38a761a00fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841368, don't leak the old AttrArray::Impl, r=peterv, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183303", "files": ["dom/base/AttrArray.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c6b948333ca7fdb72e6680835bbb15070c631909", "parents": ["3a68be3f458d47d42871857cc4790d32bb0ef8a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842221 - Simplify ThinArc and friends. r=boris, a=dsmith\n\nThinArc is way more complex than it needs to be, and miri complains\nabout various things when using the selectors crate with it.\n\nThis doesn't fully fix miri, but it gets much closer. ThinArc becomes\njust an alias for Arc\u003cHeaderSlice\u003c\u003e\u003e. This allows to simplify the\nbindings to ArcSlice too, since now the existing Arc\u003c\u003e code can just be\nused.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183011", "files": ["layout/style/ServoStyleConstsInlines.h", "servo/components/selectors/builder.rs", "servo/components/selectors/parser.rs", "servo/components/servo_arc/lib.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs", "servo/components/style_traits/arc_slice.rs", "servo/components/to_shmem/lib.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/cbindgen.toml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6a9d93873b8ad01a5b0c0b87f443fc9673fee907", "parents": ["c6b948333ca7fdb72e6680835bbb15070c631909"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843076 - Use data_mut in HeaderSlice::drop(), a=dsmith\n\nTentative, but it is more correct and made miri happier.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183625", "files": ["servo/components/servo_arc/lib.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6e1129ed5f135f15f574adc8e459f946e26473a3", "parents": ["6a9d93873b8ad01a5b0c0b87f443fc9673fee907"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 1: Implement NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nWraps an nsIInputStream if it's not async, for blobs for example.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178358", "files": ["dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b1f71c39a66b18d28bf5869cc612b95da20c06be", "parents": ["6e1129ed5f135f15f574adc8e459f946e26473a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 2: Implement ReadableStream::MaybeGetInputStreamIfUnread r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nAll existing GetBodyStreamHolder call is consciously done on unread streams, either to simply detect nsIInputStream-based streams or to get the internal nsIInputStream. The function can directly return nsIInputStream to fulfill the existing purposes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178359", "files": ["dom/base/BodyStream.cpp", "dom/fetch/Fetch.cpp", "dom/fetch/Response.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.h", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1b1d9b00302e16516956152d98a45fa9d08133b0", "parents": ["b1f71c39a66b18d28bf5869cc612b95da20c06be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 3: Use NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms for Blob::Stream() r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179074", "files": ["dom/file/Blob.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c32497e98b2ffa2646eb00d176c58a0e57a51371", "parents": ["1b1d9b00302e16516956152d98a45fa9d08133b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 4: Use NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms for FetchBody::GetBody() r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179075", "files": ["dom/fetch/Fetch.cpp", "dom/fetch/Fetch.h", "dom/fetch/Response.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9a92dae8f0ba118085e0f99d7e0453439be6b91a", "parents": ["c32497e98b2ffa2646eb00d176c58a0e57a51371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 5: Remove BodyStream in favor of InputToReadableStreamAlgorithms r=smaug a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178360", "files": ["dom/base/BodyStream.cpp", "dom/base/BodyStream.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/streams/ByteStreamHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "264aee482837e803cd07fb28e0e98e5147dac6fe", "parents": ["9a92dae8f0ba118085e0f99d7e0453439be6b91a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689799412, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "42": {"changesets": [{"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out 5 changesets (bug 1811882) for causing build bustages in Fetch.cpp a=backout\n\nBacked out changeset 264aee482837 (bug 1811882)\nBacked out changeset 9a92dae8f0ba (bug 1811882)\nBacked out changeset c32497e98b2f (bug 1811882)\nBacked out changeset 1b1d9b00302e (bug 1811882)\nBacked out changeset b1f71c39a66b (bug 1811882)", "files": ["dom/base/BodyStream.cpp", "dom/base/BodyStream.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/fetch/Fetch.cpp", "dom/fetch/Fetch.h", "dom/fetch/Response.cpp", "dom/file/Blob.cpp", "dom/streams/ByteStreamHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.h", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "295f051c5c5e6e0d07850587bffe7698c6b614b1", "parents": ["264aee482837e803cd07fb28e0e98e5147dac6fe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689802309, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ctuns@mozilla.com"}, "43": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1837163: Use correct ATK text attribute names. r=eeejay, a=dsmith\n\nGecko uses different text attribute names to ATK.\nSome of the values are also in a different format.\nThis detail was missed in the conversion from nsPersistentProperties to AccAttributes (bug 1714390), thus regressing text attributes for ATK.\nTher old conversion code added additional attributes, mangled strings, etc.\nAccAttributes allows us to do better than this, so refactor the code accordingly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183156", "files": ["accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceText.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "31e675346c0b685d029df6a392dab6a7b1756754", "parents": ["295f051c5c5e6e0d07850587bffe7698c6b614b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842160: Support the LABELLED_BY/LABEL_FOR relations on HTML figure/figcaption for RemoteAccessible. r=morgan, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183316", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessibleBase.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_relations_002.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3d5ea64695977f99dd0c6dc3638dfc6b5449b148", "parents": ["31e675346c0b685d029df6a392dab6a7b1756754"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francesco Lodolo (:flod) \u003cflod@lodolo.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1844418 - Update l10n-changesets.json for ESR115, r=RyanVM, a=dsmith, l10n=flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184023", "files": ["browser/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9c3c87175ec41946a06c80ba8dce5b74476e7faf", "parents": ["3d5ea64695977f99dd0c6dc3638dfc6b5449b148"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689807289, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "44": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 1: Implement NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nWraps an nsIInputStream if it's not async, for blobs for example.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178358", "files": ["dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "196f38bbae6858a3c26fc0d02d6c9516c637e141", "parents": ["9c3c87175ec41946a06c80ba8dce5b74476e7faf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 2: Implement ReadableStream::MaybeGetInputStreamIfUnread r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nAll existing GetBodyStreamHolder call is consciously done on unread streams, either to simply detect nsIInputStream-based streams or to get the internal nsIInputStream. The function can directly return nsIInputStream to fulfill the existing purposes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178359", "files": ["dom/base/BodyStream.cpp", "dom/fetch/Fetch.cpp", "dom/fetch/Response.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.h", "dom/streams/UnderlyingSourceCallbackHelpers.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "450dd73bab181843cfb9f07f2f1e0c1966969644", "parents": ["196f38bbae6858a3c26fc0d02d6c9516c637e141"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 3: Use NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms for Blob::Stream() r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179074", "files": ["dom/file/Blob.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b35c07d7f0f0851ed0ea339d431b965e4d1e72f6", "parents": ["450dd73bab181843cfb9f07f2f1e0c1966969644"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 4: Use NonAsyncInputToReadableStreamAlgorithms for FetchBody::GetBody() r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179075", "files": ["dom/fetch/Fetch.cpp", "dom/fetch/Fetch.h", "dom/fetch/Response.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "675f09c574dd6329542b852dd539cd9774061eb4", "parents": ["b35c07d7f0f0851ed0ea339d431b965e4d1e72f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1811882 - Part 5: Remove BodyStream in favor of InputToReadableStreamAlgorithms r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178360", "files": ["dom/base/BodyStream.cpp", "dom/base/BodyStream.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/streams/ByteStreamHelpers.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ff95b31e07df76dcc2855f6299ce8696126b4aac", "parents": ["675f09c574dd6329542b852dd539cd9774061eb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1819124 - Mark \"native\" stream constructors as MOZ_CAN_RUN_SCRIPT_BOUNDARY r=smaug, a=dsmith\n\nIt's marked as can-run-script because of StartCallback, but Underlying{Source/Sink}AlgorithmsWrapper::StartCallback is empty and thus can't run any scripts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D178356", "files": ["dom/streams/ReadableStream.cpp", "dom/streams/ReadableStream.h", "dom/streams/WritableStream.cpp", "dom/streams/WritableStream.h", "dom/streams/WritableStreamDefaultController.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportReceiveStream.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportSendStream.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1d4642188cfe74e28928e8310f55972cfa64fe85", "parents": ["ff95b31e07df76dcc2855f6299ce8696126b4aac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184087", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "028df68a461b226a7db66eccd88654f36bec1494", "parents": ["1d4642188cfe74e28928e8310f55972cfa64fe85"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689856118, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "45": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dianna Smith \u003cdsmith@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1833876. a=dsmith\ncommit 966ecd271572edc7189bf3654d218ec4253fdeaf\nAuthor: Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e\nDate:   Tue May 30 13:52:14 2023 -0400\n\n    Bug 1833876.\n\n    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179483", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasUtils.cpp", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvas.cpp", "dom/canvas/OffscreenCanvas.h", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "282fb45e9af383a029d089788347c1d36423ecab", "parents": ["028df68a461b226a7db66eccd88654f36bec1494"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ganna \u003cannhermy@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1814424 - Use moz-support-link for the helpButton link in preferences.xhtml r=tgiles,settings-reviewers,Gijs, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D179849", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/preferences.js", "browser/components/preferences/preferences.xhtml", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-support-link/moz-support-link.mjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a43b3b04882fde7f7c9afcd08bd6aa6e30f04817", "parents": ["282fb45e9af383a029d089788347c1d36423ecab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Giles \u003ctgiles@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840953 - Fix moz-support-link overwriting assigned data-l10n-name. r=mstriemer, a=dsmith\n\nAllows moz-support-link to have data-l10n-name assigned to it via\nFluent file without overwriting the data-l10n-name attribute.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183418", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_support_link.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-support-link/moz-support-link.mjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "095e8e07640f056045591a8fc73f2a4949a24a3e", "parents": ["a43b3b04882fde7f7c9afcd08bd6aa6e30f04817"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1844232 - Fix OpenH264 process crash by disabling logging by default. r=webrtc-reviewers,ng, a=dsmith\n\nThe updated OpenH264 plugin appears to sometimes crashes during logging.\nWe do not need this logging enabled by default, as the user should\nexplicitly opt into it for testing purposes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184024", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/WebrtcGmpVideoCodec.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "45b0ab0fa525bdbfff26d711df4b7d9744055f11", "parents": ["095e8e07640f056045591a8fc73f2a4949a24a3e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1689877110, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "46": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1841682 - (ESR115) Simplify post barrier for MStoreElementHole and MArrayPush. r=iain!, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184210", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.h", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cef9812a2701c45133066d71e950bf565c9ba26e", "parents": ["45b0ab0fa525bdbfff26d711df4b7d9744055f11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1816677 - Allow to retry diffrent IP family for Http/3, r=necko-reviewers,valentin, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D180679", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsUDPSocket.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEntry.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEntry.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/DnsAndConnectSocket.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpConnectionUDP.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ObliviousHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsIHttpChannelInternal.idl", "netwerk/protocol/viewsource/nsViewSourceChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_http3_dns_retry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9de50c08d971142b504872e673601a4d57f4a360", "parents": ["cef9812a2701c45133066d71e950bf565c9ba26e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1690140908, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "47": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1842860: Increase stack size in WifiMonitor on MacOS r=haik,necko-reviewers,kershaw, a=dsmith\n\nWe have been seeing the stack issue from bug 1776210, but on MacOS 10.12 Sierra.  We are increasing stack size for all versions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183611", "files": ["netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.cpp", "netwerk/wifi/nsWifiMonitor.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "06ae187d51c68cd88a546e424e070847c6f7a12b", "parents": ["9de50c08d971142b504872e673601a4d57f4a360"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1844674 - Account for screen slop when calculating available top/left in extension window apis. r=extension-reviewers,robwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184239", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-windows.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1a95a0b7dffa7178da7b7a4502b17670cca86be4", "parents": ["06ae187d51c68cd88a546e424e070847c6f7a12b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alwu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1833786 - postpone creating a decoder if the proxy isn't ready, when the info changes from unencrypted to encrypted. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond,azebrowski, a=dsmith\n\nThis can happen on Clear Lead situation, where the playback starts with\nthe unencrypted data, then changes to encrypted playback later.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184027", "files": ["dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d93418e81bb4387bb96b7e873ef65efc33861052", "parents": ["1a95a0b7dffa7178da7b7a4502b17670cca86be4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr115 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update, r=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184361", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cbd60d901baaed5e5c391477be439f09ea1f3add", "parents": ["d93418e81bb4387bb96b7e873ef65efc33861052"], "tags": []}], "date": 1690199000, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "48": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843003 - Allow overriding Content-Length using ^headers^ file. r=alwu,necko-reviewers,kershaw, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183735", "files": ["netwerk/test/httpserver/httpd.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4a5249e25b9dd60230673e1b9b3a0d8b027aa8e9", "parents": ["cbd60d901baaed5e5c391477be439f09ea1f3add"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843003 - Keep track of how much padding has been stripped, and don't trim more than necessary. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183736", "files": ["dom/media/mp3/MP3Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/mp3/MP3Demuxer.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "65288babe6828f63b3170d255217e5bec19e0275", "parents": ["4a5249e25b9dd60230673e1b9b3a0d8b027aa8e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843003 - Test that typical mp3 broadcast work well. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183737", "files": ["dom/media/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/media/test/single-xing-header-no-content-length.mp3", "dom/media/test/single-xing-header-no-content-length.mp3^headers^", "dom/media/test/test_mp3_broadcast.html", "dom/media/test/two-xing-header-no-content-length.mp3", "dom/media/test/two-xing-header-no-content-length.mp3^headers^"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3afa7cfe14a31b26b568b449b2a52e84b7f8013", "parents": ["65288babe6828f63b3170d255217e5bec19e0275"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843960 - Skip over ID3v1 tag in the middle of mp3 bytestreams. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183998", "files": ["dom/media/mp3/MP3FrameParser.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7422e924e62433249b88bcd2b221e89bf178faae", "parents": ["e3afa7cfe14a31b26b568b449b2a52e84b7f8013"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1843960 - Add a mp3 file that has an ID3v1 tag after a very long ID3v2 tag. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D183997", "files": ["dom/media/test/id3v1afterlongid3v2.mp3", "dom/media/test/manifest.js", "dom/media/test/mochitest.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "63130d62c00393b7d6a14f232074ca3c750d1e0e", "parents": ["7422e924e62433249b88bcd2b221e89bf178faae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1844741 - Consistently use remaining padding when trimming mp3. r=alwu, a=dsmith\n\nCreating the file was made in the following way:\n- Create a VBR file\n- Modify the padding field so that it spans multiple packets (greater than 1152\nframes in this case)\n- Copy and paste the last mp3 packet (starting with 0xfffd) multiple times so\nthat more packets are found after having trimmed the last packet (marked as\nEOS).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D184213", "files": ["dom/media/mp3/MP3Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/test/manifest.js", "dom/media/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/media/test/padding-spanning-multiple-packets.mp3", "dom/media/test/test_mp3_broadcast.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "662ab9287f0197d9799c6c15fde1ec07bfce8865", "parents": ["63130d62c00393b7d6a14f232074ca3c750d1e0e"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_115_1_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_115_1_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1690202453, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}}
}";